      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To investigate the effects of lipid-modulation and antiplatelet treatment on the expression of endothelial lipase (EL) of patients with coronary artery disease (CAD), and investigate the role of EL in the development of CAD."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "One hundred and fifty-seven cases were divided into three groups according to clinical manifestations and the results of coronary artery angiography: control group (n=41) with more than one risk factors of CAD and the vessel lesions was <30%; stable angina pectoris (SAP) group (n=55); acute coronary syndrome (ACS) group (n=61). The EL positive cell rate was measured 2 weeks after cessation of lipid-modulation and aspirin treatment, and 6 months after treatment with simvastatin and/or aspirin. The drug was ceased for the complications or not tolerance for the treatment."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "Except the patients in control group with aspirin treatment, the EL positive cell rate was significantly decreased among other groups [control group with simvastatin: (3.93±0.87)% vs. (5.28±1.05)%, SAP group: (8.16±2.11)% vs. (15.12±2.53)%, ACS group: (13.93±3.22)% vs. (38.44±4.36)%; SAP group with aspirin: (10.57±4.07)% vs. (14.66±2.29)%, ACS group: (18.28±5.14)% vs. (40.27±3.96)%; control group with aspirin and simvastatin: (3.13±0.87)% vs. (5.33±1.25)%, SAP group: (5.68±2.20)% vs. (14.89±2.15)%, ACS group: (7.81±3.96)% vs. (39.27±5.17)%, P<0.05 or P<0.01]."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The treatment with lipid-modulation and/or antiplatelet drug may significantly decrease the expression of EL, implying that EL participates in the progression of CAD."
        }
      ]},
